WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:04.560
It’s been a week since Johan went back to Prussia.

00:04.560 --> 00:08.120
Everything is back to its normal fun.

00:08.960 --> 00:13.300
But I can’t forget what he taught me...

00:13.300 --> 00:18.410
that I’m Ayako-san’s boyfriend, and that’s very special.

00:36.140 --> 00:41.260
Today I shout out another good morning courageously

00:41.260 --> 00:46.560
The sparkling chime of hope is resounding

00:47.050 --> 00:52.140
The gentle sun is always

00:52.140 --> 00:57.660
Blessing the late coming sensation of the two of them

00:57.950 --> 01:02.880
To fall in love with a goddess is the best!

01:03.090 --> 01:12.950
Even if she is a beatrice I can't control this throbbing feeling

01:12.950 --> 01:13.800
L·O·V·E

01:13.800 --> 01:15.550
I love you MA·MO·RU!

01:15.550 --> 01:17.090
These overflowing feelings

01:17.090 --> 01:19.790
Take them high into the sky

01:19.790 --> 01:24.680
Please grant me my dazzling and sparkling dream

01:24.680 --> 01:26.480
That's right MA·MO·RU!

01:26.480 --> 01:28.010
Only for you

01:28.010 --> 01:30.680
I will show you my power of miracles

01:30.680 --> 01:32.950
I will surely, surely swear

01:32.950 --> 01:38.900
I will not end my Shining Love

01:54.640 --> 01:57.590
Kikukawa-san, thank you for everything.

01:57.590 --> 01:59.500
You’re welcome.

01:59.500 --> 02:02.160
The mistress has been so much happier since

02:02.160 --> 02:04.620
she began attending school with you.

02:04.620 --> 02:07.610
It’s been a big help to me, too.

02:07.610 --> 02:11.430
Kikukawa, don’t you think you’re
talking too much this morning?

02:11.430 --> 02:12.550
Of course.

02:12.550 --> 02:14.630
Well, I’ll be off.

02:14.630 --> 02:15.900
Goodbye.

02:15.900 --> 02:16.730
Yes.

02:16.730 --> 02:19.030
Have a nice day, you two.

02:21.960 --> 02:22.760
Mamoru...

02:23.580 --> 02:25.030
What?

02:25.030 --> 02:30.100
Um... There wasn’t any special reason,

02:30.100 --> 02:33.700
but I worked extra hard on lunch today.

02:33.700 --> 02:38.880
There’s no real reason. I just got up a little early...

02:38.880 --> 02:40.510
And so, Mamoru...

02:40.510 --> 02:43.200
Yes, I’m looking forward to it.

02:47.000 --> 02:48.200
Ayako-san?

02:48.200 --> 02:50.770
I-It’s nothing!

02:50.770 --> 02:51.850
Wait!

02:51.850 --> 02:52.620
Ayako-san!

02:55.290 --> 02:56.090
Ayako-san...

02:57.350 --> 03:00.790
Really, your smile... It’s not fair.

03:02.970 --> 03:06.300
See you at lunch, then.

03:12.100 --> 03:15.010
<i>Today’s going to be another wonderful day.</i>

03:15.010 --> 03:18.980
<i>I’ll be late.</i>

03:21.740 --> 03:22.650
What?

03:24.110 --> 03:26.480
<i>Why is there a black cat here?</i>

03:26.480 --> 03:27.560
<i>Well, whatever.</i>

03:31.290 --> 03:32.850
<i>Wh-What?</i>

03:32.850 --> 03:35.270
<i>That’s an unlucky way to start the day...</i>

03:35.270 --> 03:37.730
Good morning, Mamoru-san.

03:39.030 --> 03:40.780
Hi, good morning.

03:43.860 --> 03:45.580
Who are you...

03:45.580 --> 03:50.280
You really had a fall. Are you OK?

03:52.000 --> 03:56.700
<i>This voice... This speaking pattern...</i>

03:57.910 --> 03:58.750
Impossible!

03:59.080 --> 04:00.390
What?

04:00.390 --> 04:01.300
Is something wrong?

04:05.960 --> 04:07.800
Vice-President?

04:10.560 --> 04:15.570
The Most Beautiful Hair in the World

04:15.570 --> 04:18.150
2 Hours Earlier . . . . . .

04:20.610 --> 04:22.310
It’s done!

04:25.920 --> 04:28.750
How beautiful!

04:28.750 --> 04:30.760
Good morning, Shione.

04:30.760 --> 04:33.250
I see you’re trying another amazing hairstyle today.

04:33.250 --> 04:36.000
You look like a frozen yogurt monster.

04:36.000 --> 04:39.270
What’s wrong with you this morning, Brother?

04:39.270 --> 04:40.840
What does that mean?

04:40.840 --> 04:42.710
Something like,

04:42.710 --> 04:46.540
“When I’m outside, I’ll have to
pretend not to know you.”

04:47.270 --> 04:50.390
What do you think my hair is?

04:51.880 --> 04:54.810
I can’t believe it!

04:54.810 --> 04:58.620
Always, always... My brother,
Ayako, and everyone else.

04:59.240 --> 05:03.070
Why can’t they understand my sense of aesthetics?

05:07.890 --> 05:10.660
<i>No!</i>

05:11.050 --> 05:11.660
Shione?

05:11.660 --> 05:12.760
Is something wrong?

05:17.650 --> 05:20.940
It’s fine... Don’t worry about it...

05:21.530 --> 05:25.730
Would you go to school alone
this morning? I’ll catch up.

05:26.370 --> 05:29.570
Sure... That’s fine.

05:30.060 --> 05:31.220
But are you OK?

05:31.220 --> 05:32.790
Yes...

05:32.790 --> 05:33.670
See you.

05:36.450 --> 05:39.100
<i>If this is true...</i>

05:39.100 --> 05:44.630
<i>For my own future’s sake, I must
resolve myself to the challenge.</i>

05:44.630 --> 05:46.370
And thus . . .

05:46.370 --> 05:49.550
You really are the Vice-President, right?

05:49.550 --> 05:51.860
If something’s bothering you, please tell me!

05:51.860 --> 05:56.910
If there’s anything I can do, I’ll help.

05:56.910 --> 05:59.950
So... Um... Oh, right!

05:59.950 --> 06:01.810
Do you have a fever?

06:01.810 --> 06:03.550
What does that mean?

06:03.550 --> 06:06.650
And why do you have small tears in your eyes?

06:07.090 --> 06:08.450
Oh, Mamoru-kun!

06:08.450 --> 06:09.430
Morning!

06:09.430 --> 06:12.050
What was that scream?

06:12.050 --> 06:14.590
You were yelling, “Vice-President”!

06:15.370 --> 06:17.720
Is something wrong with Shione?

06:17.720 --> 06:19.680
Good morning, Mitsuki!

06:19.680 --> 06:21.420
It’s nice weather today, isn’t it?

06:21.420 --> 06:23.170
Hey, good morning...

06:32.100 --> 06:33.480
That’s the Vice-President?

06:33.480 --> 06:36.510
That’s Sudou Shione’s hair,

06:36.510 --> 06:38.520
one of the Seven Mysteries
of East-B University High?!

06:39.740 --> 06:40.630
Impossible...

06:40.630 --> 06:41.390
It’s a curse!

06:41.390 --> 06:42.320
A curse!

06:42.320 --> 06:44.800
Something terrible is going to happen!

06:44.800 --> 06:47.020
Once upon a time, there was an old man who looked

06:44.800 --> 06:47.020
Watanabe fainted!

06:47.020 --> 06:49.130
like an old woman, and an old woman who looked

06:47.020 --> 06:49.130
Someone get the school nurse!

06:49.130 --> 06:52.550
like an old man, and they lived happily ever after...

06:53.220 --> 06:54.200
Hey!

06:54.200 --> 06:55.200
What’s wrong?

07:00.040 --> 07:01.780
Even the beatrice is shocked.

07:02.570 --> 07:04.810
Good morning, Mamoru-kun.

07:04.810 --> 07:06.680
I heard a mighty scream.

07:06.680 --> 07:07.790
What’s wrong?

07:07.790 --> 07:10.110
President, well...

07:10.110 --> 07:13.220
Brother, good timing.

07:13.220 --> 07:15.560
Would you calm everyone down?

07:16.730 --> 07:18.130
“Brother”?

07:18.130 --> 07:21.990
I wish I had a cute sister like you...

07:21.990 --> 07:25.690
My sister’s hairstyle and clothes
are practically criminal, you see.

07:26.410 --> 07:28.200
Brother...

07:28.200 --> 07:33.600
President, look at her closely. Really closely.

07:39.140 --> 07:41.040
What’s wrong with Shione?

07:41.040 --> 07:42.170
Nothing!

07:43.130 --> 07:44.120
Really?

07:44.120 --> 07:45.760
Shione?

07:45.760 --> 07:49.610
I never thought I’d see you
with an actual human hairstyle!

07:52.200 --> 07:56.390
I’m so happy to have such a cute little sister...

07:57.280 --> 07:58.430
Brother!

07:58.430 --> 08:00.430
If you keep that up, I’ll seriously hit you.

08:00.430 --> 08:03.080
What do you think—

08:03.460 --> 08:04.580
It’s real.

08:04.580 --> 08:05.890
I can’t believe it.

08:05.890 --> 08:07.580
Of course.

08:07.580 --> 08:09.630
Which means...

08:09.630 --> 08:11.130
President.

08:11.130 --> 08:12.740
Yes.

08:12.740 --> 08:16.810
This is the greatest mystery in the history of East-B.

08:16.810 --> 08:19.430
Some vast conspiracy is afoot.

08:19.790 --> 08:22.150
Otherwise, Shione would never have been able

08:22.150 --> 08:24.870
to understand what a real human hairstyle looks like.

08:24.870 --> 08:25.790
Um...

08:25.790 --> 08:28.360
You can feel it, too. Right, Mamoru?

08:28.360 --> 08:31.640
The surprise and confusion of the beatrice...

08:31.640 --> 08:32.460
Yes.

08:32.460 --> 08:35.590
At this rate, the beatrice’s unease will transfer

08:35.590 --> 08:39.080
to the people’s hearts, filling the world with chaos!

08:39.080 --> 08:39.950
Um...

08:40.300 --> 08:43.470
I must find out the truth behind this mystery!

08:43.470 --> 08:48.230
I swear on my name, Takasu Ayako,
Head of the East-B University Security Group!

08:50.040 --> 08:51.720
This isn’t working.

08:51.720 --> 08:54.060
Sudou Shione Hairstyle Crisis Response HQ

08:54.060 --> 08:58.240
Thirty percent of the students’ shoelaces have broken.

08:58.240 --> 09:01.060
It’s dealt a huge blow to the sports clubs.

09:01.060 --> 09:02.310
Oh, my god!

09:02.310 --> 09:07.600
Ikeda, the math teacher, was almost attacked by a giant flock of crows!

09:07.600 --> 09:09.610
Oh, my god!

09:09.610 --> 09:12.100
The Lindgren Bell wouldn’t stop ringing.

09:12.100 --> 09:14.570
It took ten students to finally stop it.

09:14.570 --> 09:17.040
Oh, no. I won’t get back in time.

09:17.040 --> 09:19.870
How unlucky... How terrifying.

09:21.650 --> 09:22.590
Don’t cry.

09:22.590 --> 09:24.620
It’s OK!

09:24.620 --> 09:29.550
Blah Blah Blah

09:26.670 --> 09:29.550
Everyone, you really have too much free time.

09:30.710 --> 09:35.720
First, we must discover why Shione
straightened her hair.

09:35.720 --> 09:36.680
Yes.

09:36.680 --> 09:40.460
Not out of curiosity or a desire for fun,
but for Shione’s sake.

09:41.870 --> 09:44.640
Hypothesis One

09:42.150 --> 09:43.000
Then...

09:43.000 --> 09:44.640
Here’s my first hypothesis.

09:44.640 --> 09:48.840
Is Shione keeping a cute chihuahua,
with big wet eyes at home?

09:48.840 --> 09:51.140
No. No, she isn’t...

09:51.140 --> 09:56.940
I have a hypothesis I’ve been
mulling over for the past year...

09:56.940 --> 10:01.730
That Shione’s hairstyle reflects her
interior mental state.

10:02.650 --> 10:05.620
Yes, when she’s upset, it stands up straight.

10:05.620 --> 10:07.990
When she’s happy, it waves.

10:07.990 --> 10:08.670
And...

10:07.990 --> 10:12.160
Here Lies Chiro

10:10.040 --> 10:12.170
Now that she’s lost her beloved chihuahua,

10:12.580 --> 10:16.430
the overwhelming sadness straightened her hair!

10:17.710 --> 10:19.270
Too sad!

10:19.270 --> 10:21.490
No, she really doesn’t have a chihuahua.

10:21.490 --> 10:23.110
Rest in peace.

10:24.930 --> 10:26.110
OK,

10:26.110 --> 10:27.100
hypothesis two!

10:27.100 --> 10:29.880
It’s a message from outer space.

10:31.730 --> 10:32.770
Outer space?

10:32.770 --> 10:37.530
It’s a message to Earthlings who’ve
gone rotten to “straighten up.”

10:35.490 --> 10:40.160
Straighten
up!

10:37.530 --> 10:41.670
And the Vice-President’s hair picked it up.

10:41.540 --> 10:44.860
Vice-President’s Hair = Antenna

10:41.670 --> 10:44.860
In other words, her hair is an antenna.

10:44.860 --> 10:46.070
Great.

10:46.070 --> 10:48.210
How sad, Shione-san!

10:48.560 --> 10:51.000
Look at her. She’s so lonely...

10:52.040 --> 10:53.040
How...

10:55.040 --> 10:55.880
How sour.

10:56.490 --> 10:57.940
Hypothesis three!

10:57.940 --> 11:03.720
Shione undid her hair to make a
secret wish she had come true!

11:03.720 --> 11:06.490
And that fervent wish is...

11:06.960 --> 11:08.270
That fervent wish is...

11:08.740 --> 11:10.940
The defeat of the Witch Beatrice, isn’t it?

11:10.940 --> 11:11.980
Yes!

11:14.250 --> 11:16.160
That seems possible!

11:16.160 --> 11:17.540
Right?

11:17.540 --> 11:19.820
How noble, Shione-san!

11:21.790 --> 11:23.160
Hypothesis four.

11:23.160 --> 11:27.970
I think it’s some evil conspiracy. I really do.

11:27.970 --> 11:29.870
Evil?

11:29.870 --> 11:30.960
Yes.

11:30.960 --> 11:35.210
Fax Fax Fax Fax

11:31.220 --> 11:32.010
Fax!

11:32.010 --> 11:35.210
Someone’s blackmailing her.

11:35.210 --> 11:37.640
If it’s something she couldn’t even tell me,

11:37.640 --> 11:41.190
then it’s something that would mean

11:41.190 --> 11:45.640
she could never show her face outside again.

11:45.970 --> 11:51.900
Her hairstyle may be a disguise,
an attempt to fool her blackmailer!

11:51.900 --> 11:53.530
Maybe...

11:54.980 --> 11:56.440
Hypothesis five!

11:56.970 --> 11:58.610
Listen to my idea!

11:58.610 --> 11:59.900
Yes, sir!

12:00.590 --> 12:01.910
It’s...

12:03.450 --> 12:04.380
love!

12:08.220 --> 12:09.220
What?

12:09.220 --> 12:10.560
Love...

12:10.560 --> 12:11.950
She’s in love!

12:12.500 --> 12:14.690
And thus, she changed.

12:15.520 --> 12:17.040
I’m sure of it!

12:20.570 --> 12:22.090
Shione in love?

12:23.720 --> 12:25.460
No way!

12:25.460 --> 12:27.030
Shione in love!

12:27.490 --> 12:28.860
Never!

12:28.860 --> 12:30.190
No, it may be possible.

12:31.140 --> 12:33.370
The oranges were yummy.
Goodbye.
Shione

12:34.460 --> 12:35.800
Hi.

12:38.050 --> 12:41.010
U-Uh, I’m sorry.

12:41.010 --> 12:43.780
You don’t have to apologize.

12:44.720 --> 12:47.260
Anyway, come in.

12:48.620 --> 12:50.870
So, what is it?

12:50.870 --> 12:52.950
That’s not like you...

12:52.950 --> 12:55.370
Running off home.

12:55.370 --> 13:02.250
I just couldn’t put up with that stupid,
unrealistic talk anymore.

13:03.980 --> 13:05.760
Shione...

13:05.760 --> 13:07.710
Don’t worry.

13:07.710 --> 13:11.080
I’ll help you with your love problems.

13:11.080 --> 13:12.340
No!

13:12.340 --> 13:14.270
I’ll make this clear—

13:14.270 --> 13:15.170
Yes.

13:15.170 --> 13:16.450
It’s not love.

13:16.450 --> 13:18.100
It’s a crime.

13:18.100 --> 13:21.950
It’s blackmail by a group of cowardly terrorists.

13:22.460 --> 13:25.790
Oh, what a terrifying world we live in.

13:26.550 --> 13:27.690
Oh, hey, President.

13:27.690 --> 13:28.830
Hi.

13:30.270 --> 13:30.950
Then...

13:31.290 --> 13:33.460
Yes, let us begin!

13:36.520 --> 13:37.590
Ayako-san?

13:37.590 --> 13:39.050
Stay still!

13:39.050 --> 13:40.920
Shione, please do this.

13:40.920 --> 13:43.380
It’s up to us to discover the truth!

13:43.380 --> 13:44.680
U-Um...

13:44.680 --> 13:46.120
Mamoru-kun,

13:46.120 --> 13:49.510
something terrible must’ve happened,
for Shione to straighten her hair.

13:50.150 --> 13:52.760
There’s a reason she can’t tell us,

13:52.760 --> 13:57.120
but in her heart, she’s broadcasting an SOS.

13:57.120 --> 13:59.180
Y-You think?

13:59.880 --> 14:03.810
Oh, how kind we are!

14:04.880 --> 14:07.530
Let’s start our search... I mean, investigation!

14:07.530 --> 14:08.130
Right!

14:08.130 --> 14:10.570
S-Search?

14:12.530 --> 14:14.490
First basic rule:

14:14.490 --> 14:16.560
Look the part.

14:19.500 --> 14:21.630
Now then, let’s get started.

14:21.630 --> 14:24.340
Is it OK to come in without asking?

14:24.920 --> 14:29.450
Either way... We need to find solid proof.

14:31.780 --> 14:33.890
Ayako-san, that mirror!

14:35.690 --> 14:41.330
Shione is sure to have straightened
her hair while looking in it.

14:41.330 --> 14:42.290
Yes.

14:42.290 --> 14:44.210
No doubt about it.

14:45.150 --> 14:46.580
Terrifying.

14:49.280 --> 14:52.830
The search/investigation was extremely difficult,

14:52.830 --> 14:57.540
and both Ayako-san and the President looked haggard...

14:59.610 --> 15:03.890
There’s no sign of any man here!

15:05.130 --> 15:06.360
Mamoru?

15:06.360 --> 15:07.590
What’s that?

15:07.590 --> 15:08.710
An album.

15:08.710 --> 15:09.360
Yes.

15:09.360 --> 15:10.830
Memories

15:09.940 --> 15:11.450
Second basic rule:

15:10.830 --> 15:13.260
Memory

15:11.450 --> 15:13.260
Look into their past.

15:13.260 --> 15:14.680
Right!

15:14.680 --> 15:17.430
You’re seeing if there are any
pictures of guys in there.

15:18.710 --> 15:21.870
You and the Vice-President were both really cute!

15:23.730 --> 15:26.140
Is this Ayako-san?

15:27.260 --> 15:31.230
Even when she was little, Ayako-san was pretty!

15:31.230 --> 15:33.570
That’s your grandfather, isn’t it?

15:33.570 --> 15:35.770
He really is the Prime Minister!

15:35.770 --> 15:37.520
I saw him on TV!

15:38.020 --> 15:42.120
It seems our parents knew Ayako’s grandfather.

15:42.120 --> 15:44.780
Once in a while, they let her stay here.

15:44.780 --> 15:46.540
Ayako-san’s so cute!

15:48.750 --> 15:50.180
Basic rule three:

15:50.180 --> 15:52.010
Stick to what’s at hand.

15:52.010 --> 15:53.740
We’re investigating Shione now.

15:53.740 --> 15:54.470
Right...

15:57.920 --> 16:01.330
Um, who is this woman?

16:01.330 --> 16:02.700
Old girlfriend.

16:02.700 --> 16:04.600
I see.

16:05.180 --> 16:06.550
And this?

16:06.550 --> 16:09.640
Old girlfriends two and three.

16:09.640 --> 16:11.240
You had quite a few, didn’t you?

16:11.240 --> 16:14.120
I-I don’t think that’s very nice...

16:14.120 --> 16:17.660
You like girls with long hair, don’t you?

16:18.340 --> 16:24.540
They all had long, straight hair.

16:25.780 --> 16:26.640
You’re right.

16:28.990 --> 16:31.930
<i>The President’s really freaking out.</i>

16:33.480 --> 16:37.180
So where’s the proof Shione’s in love
that we’re looking for?

16:40.180 --> 16:42.120
<i>Long hair...</i>

16:43.690 --> 16:47.620
You jerks!

16:52.840 --> 16:54.070
Oh, no!

16:54.070 --> 16:54.950
Shione-san!

16:54.950 --> 16:56.780
Brother! Ayako!

16:56.780 --> 16:57.700
You meanies!

17:00.890 --> 17:03.360
Meanies? At her age?

17:11.920 --> 17:13.440
Shione-san...

17:14.700 --> 17:18.490
Is it that strange for me to have straight hair?

17:18.490 --> 17:22.120
N-No, not at all.

17:27.290 --> 17:34.070
Why do you always wear your
hair and clothes that way?

17:34.070 --> 17:35.820
Because it’s beautiful.

17:35.820 --> 17:38.300
Y-Yeah.

17:40.590 --> 17:44.090
This is just my guess,

17:44.880 --> 17:51.820
but did all the girls the President
dated have long, straight hair?

17:52.550 --> 17:57.550
I wondered if that might be why.

18:00.150 --> 18:01.540
Shione-san?

18:01.540 --> 18:02.630
Are you OK?

18:02.630 --> 18:04.290
You fell off the swing...

18:05.440 --> 18:06.640
Brother-con?

18:06.640 --> 18:10.830
I’m not a brother-con, not really!

18:10.830 --> 18:12.710
Th-That’s right.

18:12.710 --> 18:14.010
I’m sorry.

18:14.010 --> 18:15.380
I was thinking too much.

18:16.680 --> 18:21.680
But you came the closest.

18:22.830 --> 18:28.090
You understand me better than Ayako or my brother.

18:33.420 --> 18:35.470
The stew’s looking good.

18:35.470 --> 18:37.930
I’m looking forward to it.

18:47.720 --> 18:49.600
We’re back!

18:50.040 --> 18:52.520
Welcome back, my sister!

18:52.520 --> 18:55.440
You can call me “big bro” from now on!

18:57.970 --> 18:59.280
Come on.

18:59.780 --> 19:01.150
Big bro!

19:03.860 --> 19:05.340
Stupid siblings.

19:10.930 --> 19:12.090
Well?

19:12.090 --> 19:13.170
It’s good!

19:13.170 --> 19:14.290
Really?

19:14.290 --> 19:16.190
Yeah, it’s great.

19:16.190 --> 19:18.240
Good...

19:42.250 --> 19:47.890
So everyone my brother dated has had straight hair?

19:47.890 --> 19:53.900
Makes you think that straight
hair might be really attractive.

19:53.900 --> 19:59.820
Of course, I learned my brother’s
practically blind. Right, Ayako?

19:59.820 --> 20:01.130
Secret
Night
Prince

20:01.130 --> 20:02.260
What?

20:06.330 --> 20:08.570
Oh, it’s nothing...

20:09.600 --> 20:12.930
It’s time for the Cupid of Love’s horoscope!

20:16.900 --> 20:20.070
It all started here...

20:20.530 --> 20:22.040
<i>Pisces!</i>

20:22.040 --> 20:23.610
<i>Roundabout is no good!</i>

20:24.210 --> 20:27.880
<i>Why not tell them how you feel, straight out?</i>

20:27.880 --> 20:29.800
<i>Everything straight up!</i>

20:31.860 --> 20:33.920
No!

20:34.380 --> 20:39.720
After all that, I can’t tell them I changed it
because of my horoscope.

20:39.720 --> 20:42.170
Everything’s going wrong for Pisces today.

20:42.170 --> 20:44.770
Well, life is long, and there’ll be days like that.

20:44.770 --> 20:47.030
Try to fight it, and it might get worse.

20:47.030 --> 20:49.940
Just be who you are!

20:52.220 --> 20:57.440
I knew I shouldn’t have tried a
weird hairstyle like “straight.”

20:57.690 --> 21:03.150
Oh, my, Ayako’s a Virgo...
“Unexpected happenings await!”

21:10.580 --> 21:14.100
We can finally have a peaceful school life now.

21:14.100 --> 21:16.220
What does that mean?

21:16.220 --> 21:18.230
I don’t know about that.

21:22.380 --> 21:23.360
Hello?

21:23.360 --> 21:24.330
This is Ayako.

21:24.810 --> 21:25.970
Grandfather?

21:29.460 --> 21:31.780
You’re coming back to Japan?

22:01.290 --> 22:06.970
My heart is racing and I'm going to give you

22:06.970 --> 22:12.170
This sparkling emotion

22:12.560 --> 22:18.300
The evening color is dyed into this orange shirt

22:18.360 --> 22:23.450
I catch it from behind you and my heart throbbing

22:23.560 --> 22:30.410
It's an everyday thrill just to be with you

22:30.410 --> 22:37.840
I can't say it well enough but thank you

22:37.840 --> 22:43.040
Venus Dream the hidden power

22:43.040 --> 22:49.240
This feeling will change into that power

22:49.240 --> 22:54.360
Power Dream I found what I want to protect

22:54.360 --> 23:00.770
That is your smile and your feelings

23:14.480 --> 23:17.390
Oh, my... Oh, my...

23:17.390 --> 23:21.920
I’m an old man, and I didn’t mean to come all this way.

23:21.920 --> 23:26.040
But I’d like the young people to try and aim higher, I would.

23:26.040 --> 23:29.820
A mind unrestrained by common sense goes crazy!

23:29.820 --> 23:34.000
And when you screw up, just say this, “Prime, sorry.”

23:35.130 --> 23:37.990
I don’t need a zabuton. A cushion’s fine.

23:38.980 --> 23:43.980
The Wild Prime Minister Is Here?!

23:39.270 --> 23:43.940
Next time: The Wild Prime Minister Is Here?!
